{{#each results}}
The organisation identifies, analyses, and treats the information security risks of its assets with a documented process, and the risk owners accept the residual risks.

== How to decide if this control is required

This control is required when the organisation runs an ISMS, or when NIS2 applies. The risks of a single product are assessed in its development project.

== How to implement

Document the risk management process, and set the acceptable risk level in the risk register. Identify and analyse the risks of the assets, and plan the treatment of each risk. Review the risk register at least once a year, and after significant changes or incidents.

